WEBVTT

1
00:00:39.874 --> 00:00:43.669
<i>NARRATOR: Long ago. a mythic
battle between good and evil</i>

2
00:00:43.753 --> 00:00:46.547
<i>played out in ancient China.</i>

3
00:00:46.631 --> 00:00:49.175
<i>The country was torn by civil war.</i>

4
00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:52.470
<i>with many kingdoms
struggling for land and power.</i>

5
00:00:54.931 --> 00:01:00.895
<i>But one king had a ruthless ambition
to make himself emperor by the sword.</i>

6
00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:11.405
(CLEARING THROAT)

7
00:01:23.251 --> 00:01:24.293
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

8
00:01:24.377 --> 00:01:25.670
Leave me.

9
00:01:25.753 --> 00:01:27.880
Prepare for war!

10
00:01:29.757 --> 00:01:32.969
<i>NARRATOR: The other rulers hired assassins
to kill the King</i>

11
00:01:33.052 --> 00:01:35.680
<i>before he could conquer them all.</i>

12
00:01:51.445 --> 00:01:53.906
(GRUNTING)

13
00:01:54.949 --> 00:01:56.993
(SWORDS CLASHING)

14
00:02:09.964 --> 00:02:11.007
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

15
00:02:15.177 --> 00:02:16.846
Stop! I am not harmed.

16
00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:25.813
We attack tonight!

17
00:02:27.732 --> 00:02:30.192
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

18
00:02:39.535 --> 00:02:44.123
<i>NARRATOR: Kingdom by kingdom.
his army swept away everything in its path.</i>

19
00:02:44.206 --> 00:02:48.044
<i>and anyone who resisted met a terrible fate.</i>

20
00:02:51.339 --> 00:02:52.965
<i>The country was his.</i>

21
00:02:53.049 --> 00:02:56.218
<i>He was now Emperor of All Under Heaven.</i>

22
00:02:57.887 --> 00:03:02.641
<i>He enslaved his conquered enemies
and forced them to build his Great Wall.</i>

23
00:03:02.725 --> 00:03:06.645
<i>When they were dead or useless.
he had them buried beneath it.</i>

24
00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:42.181
<i>The Emperor's mystics taught him
mastery over the five elements.</i>

25
00:03:43.307 --> 00:03:47.269
<i>fire. water. earth. wood and metal.</i>

26
00:03:47.353 --> 00:03:49.688
<i>His power seemed without limit.</i>

27
00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:56.112
<i>He was master of millions.</i>

28
00:03:56.195 --> 00:03:59.990
<i>but like the lowliest peasant.
he could not stop growing old.</i>

29
00:04:00.074 --> 00:04:01.117
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

30
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:05.287
I have too much to do for one lifetime.

31
00:04:05.454 --> 00:04:09.458
<i>NARRATOR: He needed to defeat
his last enemy. death itself</i>

32
00:04:16.924 --> 00:04:20.052
<i>One day. news came of a powerful witch</i>

33
00:04:20.136 --> 00:04:23.681
<i>who was rumored to know
the secret to eternal life.</i>

34
00:04:23.764 --> 00:04:29.019
<i>He ordered General Ming. his oldest friend
and trusted ally. to find her.</i>

35
00:04:40.448 --> 00:04:42.700
<i>The witch was named Zi Yuan.</i>

36
00:04:42.783 --> 00:04:45.953
<i>and she was nothing
like the General expected.</i>

37
00:04:54.253 --> 00:04:55.296
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

38
00:04:55.379 --> 00:04:56.630
Your Majesty...

39
00:05:02.344 --> 00:05:03.387
Rise up.

40
00:05:06.807 --> 00:05:10.227
I do not possess the secret of
immortality. my Lord...

41
00:05:10.311 --> 00:05:13.272
...but I know where to find it.

42
00:05:14.732 --> 00:05:15.774
General...

43
00:05:18.319 --> 00:05:20.112
No man is to touch her.

44
00:05:20.529 --> 00:05:24.033
She is mine.

45
00:05:29.038 --> 00:05:32.833
<i>NARRATOR: On the western border
stood the Monastery of Turf an.</i>

46
00:05:32.917 --> 00:05:36.921
<i>There was housed the greatest library
in the ancient world.</i>

47
00:05:37.004 --> 00:05:41.217
<i>and Zi Yuan was sure
the secret to eternal life was here.</i>

48
00:06:03.989 --> 00:06:05.032
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

49
00:06:05.115 --> 00:06:07.034
This is a key.

50
00:06:16.126 --> 00:06:18.879
<i>NARRATOR: It was the long lost
oracle bones.</i>

51
00:06:18.963 --> 00:06:23.300
<i>a collection of all the mystical secrets
of the ancient world.</i>

52
00:06:23.384 --> 00:06:28.931
<i>The Emperor's answer was here
along with other magic beyond imagining.</i>

53
00:06:39.024 --> 00:06:40.067
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

54
00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:42.027
You have served me well.

55
00:06:44.822 --> 00:06:47.866
I will grant you anything you desire.

56
00:06:49.326 --> 00:06:52.997
I want to spend my life with General Ming.

57
00:06:55.332 --> 00:06:56.834
Of course.

58
00:06:57.418 --> 00:06:58.460
Read.

59
00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:07.344
(CHANTING IN SANSKRIT)

60
00:07:16.061 --> 00:07:18.314
<i>NARRATOR: She cast the spell in Sanskrit.</i>

61
00:07:18.397 --> 00:07:22.443
<i>an ancient language
that the Emperor did not understand.</i>

62
00:07:27.072 --> 00:07:28.115
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

63
00:07:28.198 --> 00:07:30.618
I feel your spell working.

64
00:07:32.119 --> 00:07:37.875
I am now immortal.

65
00:07:39.335 --> 00:07:42.129
Come. I want to show you something.

66
00:07:54.475 --> 00:07:55.893
(EXCLAIMING)

67
00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:01.440
Become my queen and I will let him live.

68
00:08:01.899 --> 00:08:05.653
Do what he says! Save yourself!

69
00:08:09.657 --> 00:08:11.950
You will never keep your word.

70
00:08:13.577 --> 00:08:14.620
You are right.

71
00:08:21.418 --> 00:08:22.836
(GRUNTING)

72
00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:25.923
(GASPS)

73
00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:30.636
Now. join General Ming in hell.

74
00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.236
(SHOUTING)

75
00:08:47.319 --> 00:08:48.654
What did you do to me?

76
00:08:49.571 --> 00:08:51.782
I cursed you and your army.

77
00:09:01.458 --> 00:09:05.462
(EMPEROR GRUNTING IN PAIN)

78
00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.923
Surround the Palace!

79
00:09:08.048 --> 00:09:09.466
The Emperor is in trouble!

80
00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:28.402
<i>NARRATOR: The curse must never be lifted.</i>

81
00:09:28.485 --> 00:09:32.990
<i>or the Emperor will rise again
to enslave all of mankind.</i>

82
00:09:33.115 --> 00:09:37.953
<i>On that dark day.
there will be nothing and no one to save us.</i>

83
00:09:52.509 --> 00:09:55.471
You can run. but you can't hide.

84
00:10:02.269 --> 00:10:03.270
One o'clock.

85
00:10:03.353 --> 00:10:05.105
OXFORDSHIRE. ENGLAND
1946

86
00:10:06.023 --> 00:10:10.861
Ten o'clock. one o'clock. Ten o'clock. one...

87
00:10:10.986 --> 00:10:13.864
And this is something for grown men to do?

88
00:10:15.532 --> 00:10:18.368
(EXCLAIMING IN PAIN)

89
00:10:23.207 --> 00:10:24.458
(GRUNTING) Come on.

90
00:10:28.545 --> 00:10:29.880
(SCREAMS)

91
00:10:33.217 --> 00:10:34.802
Bite on this.

92
00:10:52.402 --> 00:10:54.488
Evy. I'm home!

93
00:10:54.571 --> 00:10:57.658
Mrs. O'Connell is at her book reading. sir.
She'll be home for dinner.

94
00:10:57.741 --> 00:11:01.495
Oh. right. Well. that's great.
'cause we're having fish.

95
00:11:04.748 --> 00:11:06.500
You didn't think I'd catch anything.
did you?

96
00:11:06.583 --> 00:11:09.086
I had the utmost confidence. sir.

97
00:11:11.255 --> 00:11:16.009
JAMESON: There's a hook in your neck. sir.
Shall I fetch the wire cutters?

98
00:11:20.931 --> 00:11:26.061
<i>RICK: Fall back! Follow me!
Move! Move! Move! Move!</i>

99
00:11:30.607 --> 00:11:32.943
<i>EVELYN: "Now safely aboard the airship
with the mummy finally vanquished.</i>

100
00:11:33.068 --> 00:11:34.111
LONDON

101
00:11:35.195 --> 00:11:37.698
<i>"Dash swept Scarlet into his arms.</i>

102
00:11:37.948 --> 00:11:43.078
"'Oh. God. Scarlet. I thought I'd lost you.'
'For a moment there. you did.'

103
00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:46.373
"Bathed in rays of golden sunlight.

104
00:11:46.456 --> 00:11:51.545
"our heroes sealed their reunion
with a kiss of timeless passion.

105
00:11:51.628 --> 00:11:55.132
"their love deeper and truer than ever."

106
00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:04.141
Mrs. O'Connell. we're all dying to know.

107
00:12:04.224 --> 00:12:07.728
is the Scarlet O'Keefe character
really based on you?

108
00:12:09.313 --> 00:12:12.649
Honestly. I can say
she's a completely different person.

109
00:12:12.733 --> 00:12:14.735
- Any more questions?
- WOMAN: Mrs. O'Connell...

110
00:12:14.818 --> 00:12:19.323
Mrs. O'Connell. is your life today
as exciting as it was before the war?

111
00:12:20.073 --> 00:12:21.074
(SIGHS)

112
00:12:21.158 --> 00:12:23.243
I wish my life were that exciting now.

113
00:12:23.327 --> 00:12:24.745
MAN: Will there be another book
in the series?

114
00:12:24.828 --> 00:12:27.414
WOMAN 2: Do you believe in happy endings?

115
00:12:28.582 --> 00:12:29.625
(EXHALES)

116
00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.586
Isn't this blissful?

117
00:12:34.755 --> 00:12:36.590
Dinner at home.

118
00:12:38.091 --> 00:12:40.302
- Every night.
- Every night.

119
00:12:41.011 --> 00:12:44.932
- Here's to retirement.
- May we stay this happy forever.

120
00:12:49.102 --> 00:12:50.145
(GULPS)

121
00:12:58.612 --> 00:13:02.532
Still no letter from Alex.
I've sent him three in the last month.

122
00:13:02.616 --> 00:13:03.784
Yeah. well. what do you expect?

123
00:13:03.867 --> 00:13:04.952
The only time we ever hear from that kid

124
00:13:05.035 --> 00:13:07.287
is when he's getting kicked out of college
or he needs more money.

125
00:13:07.371 --> 00:13:10.374
I'm sure he's just buried in his studies.

126
00:13:16.713 --> 00:13:20.968
- So. how did your book reading go?
- Oh. fine. Thank you.

127
00:13:21.843 --> 00:13:24.805
Until they asked me. "When will there
be another Mummy adventure?"

128
00:13:24.888 --> 00:13:27.474
Yeah. but you did promise the publisher
a third book.

129
00:13:27.557 --> 00:13:28.642
I know.

130
00:13:28.725 --> 00:13:33.063
But I spend my nights staring
at a blank page. completely blocked.

131
00:13:33.146 --> 00:13:38.318
We could skip dinner. and I could

132
00:13:38.402 --> 00:13:43.699
attempt to inspire you upstairs.

133
00:13:44.324 --> 00:13:47.577
Oh. that's so sweet of you. darling.

134
00:13:47.703 --> 00:13:52.332
But I'm going to sit at that typewriter
until something exciting comes out.

135
00:13:54.376 --> 00:13:56.044
Thank you.

136
00:13:58.005 --> 00:13:59.006
(EXCLAIMING DELIGHTEDLY)

137
00:13:59.089 --> 00:14:00.841
Trout. How lovely!

138
00:14:00.924 --> 00:14:02.009
(JAMESON CLEARS THROAT)

139
00:14:04.678 --> 00:14:08.348
I'm so happy you found a hobby
that doesn't involve guns.

140
00:14:09.766 --> 00:14:10.767
(CRUNCHING)

141
00:14:15.689 --> 00:14:18.859
NINGXIA PROVINCE. CHINA

142
00:14:29.453 --> 00:14:30.537
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

143
00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:32.080
Don't worry. we'll find the entrance today.

144
00:14:33.331 --> 00:14:36.126
Li Tung. what's for lunch?

145
00:14:36.251 --> 00:14:37.294
Noodle soup.

146
00:14:37.669 --> 00:14:39.129
Very good.

147
00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:47.304
ALEX: Good. Wilson's back.

148
00:14:48.805 --> 00:14:50.932
You're a couple days late. Professor.

149
00:14:51.016 --> 00:14:52.517
I was beginning to think
you'd run into bandits.

150
00:14:52.642 --> 00:14:54.603
Oh. my dear fellow.
thank you for the concern.

151
00:14:54.686 --> 00:14:56.396
- Are you thirsty?
- Oh. yes. please.

152
00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:58.523
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

153
00:14:59.691 --> 00:15:01.735
You know.
when I saw you standing up there.

154
00:15:01.818 --> 00:15:03.987
I thought I was looking at your father.

155
00:15:04.112 --> 00:15:05.822
You really are Rick O'Connell's son.

156
00:15:05.947 --> 00:15:10.744
Yeah. well. hopefully after today.
he'll be known as Alex O'Connell's father.

157
00:15:10.827 --> 00:15:13.538
What a powerful face!

158
00:15:13.663 --> 00:15:17.584
When I told my colleagues at the museum
that you had discovered the Colossus.

159
00:15:17.667 --> 00:15:19.252
they were thrilled.

160
00:15:19.336 --> 00:15:21.546
- Yes. however...
- I know.

161
00:15:21.671 --> 00:15:23.715
When am I gonna get in that tomb?

162
00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:25.842
Don't let the buggers get you down.

163
00:15:25.967 --> 00:15:28.345
It was you that discovered
the Bembridge journal.

164
00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:30.931
and with it. you'll discover the Emperor.

165
00:15:31.014 --> 00:15:34.810
- I have complete faith in you. Alex.
- Thank you. Professor.

166
00:15:35.477 --> 00:15:37.187
Thanks for believing in me.

167
00:15:37.312 --> 00:15:38.355
(MAN SHOUTS)

168
00:15:39.397 --> 00:15:42.484
We found it! We found the door!

169
00:15:44.861 --> 00:15:46.530
<i>Bad Mummy.</i>

170
00:15:48.031 --> 00:15:49.407
Yeah.

171
00:15:50.992 --> 00:15:52.869
<i>Vile Mummy?</i>

172
00:15:53.411 --> 00:15:54.496
(TYPING)

173
00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:56.665
No. <i>Cursed Mummy!</i>

174
00:15:56.915 --> 00:15:59.668
<i>Mysterious Mummy.</i>

175
00:16:01.753 --> 00:16:04.047
<i>Malignant Mummy.</i>

176
00:16:08.385 --> 00:16:10.512
Prepare to die!

177
00:16:12.222 --> 00:16:13.723
Take that!

178
00:16:22.107 --> 00:16:23.400
Rick!

179
00:16:25.235 --> 00:16:27.237
Darling. where are you?

180
00:16:37.873 --> 00:16:40.083
I'm ready to be inspired.

181
00:16:46.882 --> 00:16:50.844
Do you remember the time
the mummy had me tied down?

182
00:16:50.927 --> 00:16:54.890
And you came to save me and you cut...

183
00:16:54.973 --> 00:16:59.227
No! You tore open the ropes
is what you did.

184
00:16:59.311 --> 00:17:02.147
just as he was about to plunge his...

185
00:17:02.272 --> 00:17:04.733
(SNORING)

186
00:17:04.816 --> 00:17:06.234
Oh. rats.

187
00:17:27.589 --> 00:17:30.091
(LAUGHS)

188
00:17:33.929 --> 00:17:35.347
Watch out!

189
00:17:42.312 --> 00:17:44.814
- Emperor didn't want any houseguests.
- Yeah.

190
00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:45.982
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

191
00:17:46.107 --> 00:17:47.150
Stay together.

192
00:18:12.634 --> 00:18:14.511
Sir Colin Bembridge.

193
00:18:15.303 --> 00:18:16.721
Oh. gee...

194
00:18:17.555 --> 00:18:19.933
He went searching for this tomb
70 years ago.

195
00:18:20.016 --> 00:18:21.977
They left him like this as a warning.

196
00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:24.854
Unfortunately. this is not the dead man
that's gonna make us famous.

197
00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:26.690
Let's keep moving.

198
00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:56.690
<b>Subtitle 
 www.movieddl.me</b>

199
00:19:03.518 --> 00:19:04.894
Look at it. Alex.

200
00:19:05.937 --> 00:19:07.564
Look at it!

201
00:19:44.059 --> 00:19:46.186
(SCREAMING)

202
00:19:46.269 --> 00:19:47.729
Chu Wah!

203
00:19:47.812 --> 00:19:50.607
(WHIMPERING)

204
00:19:58.615 --> 00:20:00.283
(SHOUTS IN MANDARIN)

205
00:20:27.977 --> 00:20:29.813
(PANTING)

206
00:20:31.314 --> 00:20:32.941
- Chu Wah.
- No. no. don't. don't. don't.

207
00:20:33.024 --> 00:20:35.735
Alex. Alex. they're dead! Come on.

208
00:20:35.819 --> 00:20:38.947
This kind of danger goes with the territory.
You know that better than anyone.

209
00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:40.323
Alex!

210
00:20:44.661 --> 00:20:46.204
- Yes?
- Okay.

211
00:20:46.329 --> 00:20:47.705
- Yes?
- Yeah.

212
00:20:48.373 --> 00:20:52.919
All right. good chap. Okay. Good chap.
Oh. Jesus.

213
00:20:58.091 --> 00:21:01.511
All the warriors are facing in to this point.

214
00:21:01.594 --> 00:21:04.931
- as if awaiting an order from the Emperor.
- Well. then. where is he?

215
00:21:05.014 --> 00:21:09.602
Listen. you don't think some bloody grave
robber's beaten us to the prize. do you?

216
00:21:09.686 --> 00:21:11.396
No. he's still here.

217
00:21:11.521 --> 00:21:14.691
You see. this is a feng shui compass.

218
00:21:22.907 --> 00:21:25.452
Okay. Now. This...

219
00:21:25.535 --> 00:21:27.454
Okay. this is true north.

220
00:21:27.537 --> 00:21:31.791
but the feng shui compass
is set in the opposite direction.

221
00:21:31.875 --> 00:21:33.960
- All right. we need to realign it.
- All right.

222
00:21:34.043 --> 00:21:36.129
- All right. here we go.
- All right.

223
00:21:46.222 --> 00:21:47.724
(ALEX SCREAMS)

224
00:21:55.106 --> 00:21:58.067
(RAT SQUEAKING)

225
00:21:58.902 --> 00:22:01.112
Alex! Alex. speak to me!

226
00:22:01.613 --> 00:22:03.406
Are you all right?

227
00:22:04.574 --> 00:22:07.076
- Alex!
- I'm fine.

228
00:22:08.161 --> 00:22:10.747
Tell me. have we found the Emperor?

229
00:22:14.584 --> 00:22:15.835
Alex!

230
00:22:23.635 --> 00:22:24.886
What is it?

231
00:22:24.969 --> 00:22:27.931
It's only the greatest find since King Tut!

232
00:22:31.768 --> 00:22:35.730
"If he is awakened.
all mortals should despair."

233
00:22:35.813 --> 00:22:37.774
It's definitely him!

234
00:22:40.527 --> 00:22:41.945
(ALEX EXCLAIMS)

235
00:22:42.111 --> 00:22:44.531
Even had his concubines buried alive
with him.

236
00:22:44.614 --> 00:22:45.990
Selfish bastard.

237
00:22:46.616 --> 00:22:49.744
Hey. Professor Wilson.
you want to come down and take a look?

238
00:22:49.827 --> 00:22:52.997
Or are you so overwhelmed you can't talk?

239
00:22:55.291 --> 00:22:56.292
(THUD)

240
00:22:59.629 --> 00:23:02.799
(GRUNTING)

241
00:23:16.980 --> 00:23:18.314
Wilson!

242
00:23:45.842 --> 00:23:47.552
(PANTING)

243
00:24:29.302 --> 00:24:32.555
Let's go. Professor.
We've got a lot of work to do.

244
00:24:32.639 --> 00:24:33.681
WILSON: All right.

245
00:24:33.681 --> 00:24:33.723
WILSON: All right.

246
00:24:39.729 --> 00:24:41.356
FRY: First of all. I'd just like to say

247
00:24:41.439 --> 00:24:44.692
that the Foreign Office appreciates
all that you did during the war.

248
00:24:44.776 --> 00:24:49.113
But I've been sent to offer you
one last assignment.

249
00:24:49.822 --> 00:24:54.202
I'm afraid we've retired
from the espionage game. haven't we. dear?

250
00:24:54.285 --> 00:24:56.454
Yeah. we've... We don't do that any more.
We're finished.

251
00:24:56.579 --> 00:24:58.915
- EVELYN: Not at all.
- Completely done.

252
00:25:00.917 --> 00:25:04.128
But just out of curiosity.
what is the mission anyway?

253
00:25:04.253 --> 00:25:07.590
We need you to courier this to Shanghai.

254
00:25:09.300 --> 00:25:10.343
(EVELYN GASPS)

255
00:25:11.010 --> 00:25:14.389
- Nice piece of ice.
- It's the Eye of Shangri-La.

256
00:25:14.472 --> 00:25:17.975
If you believe the legend.
it points the way to the Pool of Eternal Life.

257
00:25:18.101 --> 00:25:20.228
It was smuggled out of China in 1940.

258
00:25:20.311 --> 00:25:23.064
Now. the government would like
to return it to the Shanghai Museum

259
00:25:23.147 --> 00:25:26.567
as a sign of good faith
to the Chinese people.

260
00:25:26.651 --> 00:25:30.571
And with your expertise in the field.
we naturally thought of you.

261
00:25:30.655 --> 00:25:33.616
Oh. we'd be so flattered.

262
00:25:35.660 --> 00:25:39.497
But Rick and I. we made a promise
to each other after the war

263
00:25:39.622 --> 00:25:42.667
that we would settle down.

264
00:25:42.792 --> 00:25:45.586
- That's right. yeah. we did. didn't we? We...
- I see.

265
00:25:45.670 --> 00:25:48.589
Well. I must admit I am a little disappointed.

266
00:25:48.673 --> 00:25:52.093
Postwar China is very dangerous.

267
00:25:52.176 --> 00:25:57.098
There are a lot of factions that would love
to get their hands on the Eye of Shangri-La.

268
00:25:57.181 --> 00:26:00.810
In lesser hands.
the Eye could be lost forever.

269
00:26:01.644 --> 00:26:03.271
We couldn't let that happen. could we?

270
00:26:03.354 --> 00:26:05.773
No. that could be bad for the world.

271
00:26:05.857 --> 00:26:08.025
- The world... Terrible.
- Yeah.

272
00:26:09.152 --> 00:26:10.695
You know. she has a brother
who lives in Shanghai.

273
00:26:10.820 --> 00:26:12.613
- Jonathan!
- Yes.

274
00:26:12.697 --> 00:26:14.574
He owns a nightclub. if I'm not mistaken.

275
00:26:14.657 --> 00:26:16.117
We have been meaning to visit. We could...

276
00:26:16.200 --> 00:26:17.493
- We should...
- ...drop in and surprise him.

277
00:26:17.577 --> 00:26:19.245
- Say hello.
- Why not?

278
00:26:19.328 --> 00:26:22.665
Does this mean
we can count on you one last time?

279
00:26:24.000 --> 00:26:25.001
Yes.

280
00:26:28.671 --> 00:26:30.423
SHANGHAI. CHINA

281
00:26:30.506 --> 00:26:32.508
CHINESE NEW YEAR. 1947

282
00:26:38.681 --> 00:26:40.349
(CAR HONKING)

283
00:26:43.186 --> 00:26:45.062
(MUSIC PLAYING)

284
00:26:55.364 --> 00:26:57.867
(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

285
00:26:59.368 --> 00:27:00.536
There we are.

286
00:27:02.205 --> 00:27:04.332
Here's to you. Princess.

287
00:27:04.415 --> 00:27:07.668
And Imhotep.
May the bugger actually stay dead.

288
00:27:07.752 --> 00:27:08.836
(TOASTING IN RUSSIAN)

289
00:27:08.920 --> 00:27:10.379
Ding-dong.

290
00:27:18.471 --> 00:27:20.932
Hi. can you buy a drink for me?

291
00:27:21.808 --> 00:27:24.727
Excuse me. Alex! Alex! You're back again.

292
00:27:24.811 --> 00:27:26.270
Come here. Alex. Let me get you a drink.

293
00:27:26.395 --> 00:27:28.898
Smooth special for the pup. huh?
The explorer.

294
00:27:29.106 --> 00:27:30.149
(LAUGHS)

295
00:27:31.067 --> 00:27:32.401
Make that two.

296
00:27:32.485 --> 00:27:35.029
Sorry. Uncle Jon. but I got a better offer.

297
00:27:35.112 --> 00:27:38.825
JONATHAN: No. no. Alex. No. look.
Listen. how can I... Come here.

298
00:27:38.908 --> 00:27:40.701
To put it in archeological terms.

299
00:27:40.785 --> 00:27:42.995
that's a tomb
in which many pharaohs have lain.

300
00:27:43.079 --> 00:27:45.998
Now. listen. listen.
just think about me for a moment. all right?

301
00:27:46.082 --> 00:27:49.877
Your discovery will go public in a few days.
and your parents are sure to find out.

302
00:27:49.961 --> 00:27:52.505
They're not gonna be happy
you've dropped out of school. And...

303
00:27:52.588 --> 00:27:56.425
Will you relax. Uncle Jon? Okay? I'm here.
They're a long way away.

304
00:27:56.509 --> 00:27:59.345
- Alex...
- Excuse me. okay?

305
00:27:59.428 --> 00:28:01.764
I have some excavation to do.

306
00:28:09.856 --> 00:28:11.274
Jonathan!

307
00:28:13.776 --> 00:28:15.403
(LAUGHS NERVOUSLY)

308
00:28:15.486 --> 00:28:18.656
You're in China! Evy. Rick.

309
00:28:18.781 --> 00:28:21.117
(STUTTERING) What are you... It's so...
I didn't even...

310
00:28:21.200 --> 00:28:24.412
Brother. how lovely to see you.

311
00:28:24.495 --> 00:28:26.247
I had no idea he was here!

312
00:28:26.330 --> 00:28:27.790
- Who was here?
- Who?

313
00:28:28.624 --> 00:28:29.667
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

314
00:28:29.792 --> 00:28:31.836
MAN: This happens every time!

315
00:28:32.795 --> 00:28:34.922
Every man in the bar!

316
00:28:35.006 --> 00:28:36.090
- Dad?
- Alex!

317
00:28:36.173 --> 00:28:37.842
MAN:I don't know what to do with you!
WOMAN: He's just a boy!

318
00:28:37.967 --> 00:28:41.262
- I can't leave the room for 10 minutes!
- I didn't... Go away! Go to hell!

319
00:28:41.345 --> 00:28:43.389
- MAN: I'm sick of it!
- Let's go get lover-boy!

320
00:28:43.472 --> 00:28:45.433
I'm gonna kill you. kid!

321
00:28:45.516 --> 00:28:47.810
Not so fast. that's my kid.

322
00:28:49.854 --> 00:28:53.149
- Mad Dog Maguire?
- Ricochet O'Connell.

323
00:28:53.649 --> 00:28:56.110
- Hey. hey.
- EVELYN: What are you doing here?

324
00:28:56.193 --> 00:28:59.071
- Alex! Sweetheart! Are you all right?
- Just a little family get-together. folks.

325
00:28:59.155 --> 00:29:02.575
Come on.
let's get back to having a good time. Music!

326
00:29:03.075 --> 00:29:04.118
How long has it been?

327
00:29:04.201 --> 00:29:07.038
Egypt. '23. French Foreign Legion.

328
00:29:08.414 --> 00:29:10.374
This guy could land a plane
on anything. you...

329
00:29:10.499 --> 00:29:13.085
- Why are you here?
- Ricochet. he had his hands all over me girl.

330
00:29:13.169 --> 00:29:15.463
Now. son or no son.
I gotta give him a beating!

331
00:29:15.546 --> 00:29:17.882
- Get out of the way. Dad.
- Sit down.

332
00:29:18.007 --> 00:29:20.718
Now as much as I'd really like you
to teach him a valuable lesson...

333
00:29:20.843 --> 00:29:22.470
His mother would be upset! Very upset.

334
00:29:22.553 --> 00:29:24.096
You have a lot of explaining to do.
young man.

335
00:29:24.180 --> 00:29:25.389
I got a wife now. and a kid.

336
00:29:25.514 --> 00:29:27.642
Things are a little bit different.
I'm sure you understand.

337
00:29:27.725 --> 00:29:29.435
- Yeah.
- Let me make it up to you.

338
00:29:30.728 --> 00:29:32.855
We're just surprised to see you here.
That's all.

339
00:29:32.939 --> 00:29:34.357
JONATHAN: Who's gonna pay
for all this damage?

340
00:29:34.440 --> 00:29:35.733
All right?

341
00:29:35.858 --> 00:29:36.859
I'm not here five minutes.

342
00:29:36.943 --> 00:29:38.819
and I'm already pulling your fanny
out of the fire.

343
00:29:38.903 --> 00:29:39.946
You're going back to college.

344
00:29:40.029 --> 00:29:43.199
How'd you think this was gonna work. Dad?
You two show up. tell me what to do?

345
00:29:43.282 --> 00:29:47.745
No. But we should sit down
and discuss this like a family.

346
00:29:47.870 --> 00:29:50.623
No offense. Mom.
but we haven't been a family in a long time.

347
00:29:50.706 --> 00:29:52.750
Hey. don't you turn your back on me. Alex!

348
00:29:52.875 --> 00:29:55.211
Alex. just... Alex. come here.

349
00:29:57.213 --> 00:29:58.714
Can you...

350
00:29:59.966 --> 00:30:02.176
Don't look at me like that.

351
00:30:02.259 --> 00:30:03.302
(SIGHS)

352
00:30:08.057 --> 00:30:10.434
- It's all your fault!
- My fault?

353
00:30:10.559 --> 00:30:12.228
You're the one
that's always smothering him.

354
00:30:12.311 --> 00:30:14.855
You couldn't leave him alone
for five minutes without wiping his nose.

355
00:30:14.939 --> 00:30:18.693
Perhaps I was overcompensating for the fact
that you never took an interest in his life.

356
00:30:18.776 --> 00:30:21.445
His life was my top priority.

357
00:30:21.570 --> 00:30:24.115
How many times did I save that kid
from breaking his neck?

358
00:30:24.240 --> 00:30:26.450
A little warmth and encouragement
would have been nice.

359
00:30:26.575 --> 00:30:29.245
I'm his father. It's implied.

360
00:30:32.415 --> 00:30:36.252
We've spent our entire lives
searching for priceless artifacts.

361
00:30:36.335 --> 00:30:37.920
and the one thing
that's most precious to us.

362
00:30:38.004 --> 00:30:39.088
we've lost.

363
00:30:40.756 --> 00:30:45.761
We can't let Alex become some stranger
in pictures on our mantle.

364
00:30:46.512 --> 00:30:48.264
- We can't let that happen.
- No. we can't.

365
00:30:48.347 --> 00:30:50.474
How are we gonna fix this?

366
00:30:52.101 --> 00:30:54.270
We need to do it together.

367
00:31:00.776 --> 00:31:05.156
PARAMILITARY OUTPOST
WESTERN CHINA

368
00:31:05.281 --> 00:31:06.991
(MACHINE GUNS FIRING)

369
00:31:28.512 --> 00:31:29.638
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

370
00:31:29.722 --> 00:31:32.516
The O'Connells are in Shanghai.

371
00:31:33.142 --> 00:31:35.603
Do they have the Eye of Shangri-La?

372
00:31:35.686 --> 00:31:38.064
Our spy says they do.

373
00:31:38.564 --> 00:31:39.648
Good.

374
00:31:39.815 --> 00:31:40.983
Assemble the troops!

375
00:31:41.067 --> 00:31:42.151
Yes sir.

376
00:31:46.655 --> 00:31:47.656
Soldiers!

377
00:31:48.240 --> 00:31:51.660
Soon all our training and sacrifice...

378
00:31:52.328 --> 00:31:54.872
will bear great fruit.

379
00:31:55.915 --> 00:31:59.168
It is my dream to raise our Emperor
from his tomb.

380
00:31:59.877 --> 00:32:03.005
Only He can bring order out of this chaos.

381
00:32:04.048 --> 00:32:05.091
Soldiers...

382
00:32:06.342 --> 00:32:10.012
tonight our great battle begins!

383
00:32:10.096 --> 00:32:11.597
(ALL CHANTING)

384
00:32:12.681 --> 00:32:15.518
(PEOPLE CHEERING)

385
00:32:21.190 --> 00:32:24.693
You know. this might have been faster
if we took a rickshaw.

386
00:32:24.777 --> 00:32:27.113
It's Chinese New Year.

387
00:32:27.196 --> 00:32:28.239
Don't you just love this country?

388
00:32:28.322 --> 00:32:31.700
They have so many extra little holidays.
and drinking is mandatory.

389
00:32:31.784 --> 00:32:34.370
I can't believe
we get to see your first big discovery.

390
00:32:34.453 --> 00:32:35.496
It's so exciting.

391
00:32:35.579 --> 00:32:38.082
Well. after last night.
I'm surprised you want to see it at all.

392
00:32:39.542 --> 00:32:42.169
JONATHAN: Listen.
I'll pick you up in about an hour.

393
00:32:42.253 --> 00:32:43.546
EVELYN: You're not coming?

394
00:32:43.629 --> 00:32:46.966
JONATHAN: No. no.
I've seen enough mummies to last a lifetime.

395
00:32:58.269 --> 00:32:59.728
There he is.

396
00:33:00.354 --> 00:33:03.774
Oh. my darling. very impressive.

397
00:33:04.733 --> 00:33:06.443
When do you get to open the sarcophagus?

398
00:33:06.527 --> 00:33:08.571
ALEX: Well.
after the official red tape has been cut.

399
00:33:08.654 --> 00:33:11.949
Do the words "rest in peace"
mean anything to you two?

400
00:33:12.032 --> 00:33:15.744
So. Mom. why don't you stick around
for the next few days.

401
00:33:15.828 --> 00:33:17.079
and we can open it together?

402
00:33:17.163 --> 00:33:18.581
I would like that very much. thanks.

403
00:33:18.664 --> 00:33:20.958
Alex. why don't you go
and tell Professor Wilson

404
00:33:21.041 --> 00:33:23.127
that we're here. You know...

405
00:33:23.210 --> 00:33:24.587
No problem. Great.

406
00:33:24.670 --> 00:33:27.840
Just don't wake the big guy up
while I'm gone.

407
00:33:34.597 --> 00:33:36.056
Hey. Alex.

408
00:33:36.682 --> 00:33:41.353
You know. this is all really. really big stuff.

409
00:33:44.773 --> 00:33:46.775
Whatever you say. Dad.

410
00:34:10.466 --> 00:34:13.344
(WHISTLING)

411
00:34:23.854 --> 00:34:25.105
What?

412
00:34:26.106 --> 00:34:31.153
You just have a certain glow about you
this evening I haven't seen in a long time.

413
00:34:32.655 --> 00:34:35.574
I guess mummies bring out the best in me.

414
00:34:36.784 --> 00:34:40.329
Take a wrong turn at Cairo?
Sorry to interrupt.

415
00:34:41.956 --> 00:34:43.916
- Roger.
- Professor Roger Wilson.

416
00:34:43.999 --> 00:34:45.334
Rick.

417
00:34:45.417 --> 00:34:48.963
You know. when Alex told me
that you had gone legit.

418
00:34:49.046 --> 00:34:51.090
I just couldn't believe my ears.

419
00:34:51.173 --> 00:34:54.885
Well. now I just pillage tombs
in the name of preservation. Evelyn.

420
00:34:54.969 --> 00:34:59.098
- Congratulations on your latest discovery.
- Alex deserves all the credit.

421
00:34:59.181 --> 00:35:01.267
He's one hell of a kid.
He's like the son I never had.

422
00:35:01.350 --> 00:35:02.685
And he's the only one we've got.

423
00:35:02.768 --> 00:35:04.812
so the next time you send him
on one of your field trips.

424
00:35:04.895 --> 00:35:06.188
you give us the heads-up first.

425
00:35:06.272 --> 00:35:08.649
Yes. yes. of course.

426
00:35:08.732 --> 00:35:12.152
And now. I believe you have
something that belongs to us.

427
00:35:12.236 --> 00:35:13.821
What's that?

428
00:35:13.904 --> 00:35:15.531
Oh. you mean this?

429
00:35:15.614 --> 00:35:16.657
(GASPS)

430
00:35:16.991 --> 00:35:19.118
(LAUGHING)

431
00:35:19.201 --> 00:35:20.703
I'm sorry...

432
00:35:22.329 --> 00:35:24.164
There. go ahead.

433
00:35:24.248 --> 00:35:26.041
All yours. Rog.

434
00:35:27.001 --> 00:35:29.586
I knew I could rely on you two.

435
00:35:31.213 --> 00:35:35.301
I'm afraid your work is not done yet.
Mr. and Mrs. O'Connell.

436
00:35:35.384 --> 00:35:39.305
I'd like to introduce you to a friend of mine.
General Yang.

437
00:35:39.388 --> 00:35:40.597
Roger!

438
00:35:41.056 --> 00:35:45.394
Well. he is the man who financed Alex's dig.
We're in this together.

439
00:35:46.270 --> 00:35:48.272
Cheek by jowl. General.

440
00:35:50.274 --> 00:35:51.775
Search him.

441
00:35:53.694 --> 00:35:57.823
No. The Eye belongs to the Chinese people.
You can't do this.

442
00:35:57.906 --> 00:36:02.411
So. Rog. you snake. how much did...

443
00:36:02.494 --> 00:36:05.289
Is it Yin and Yang? ...pay you?

444
00:36:05.372 --> 00:36:07.916
Enough to pull strings at the Foreign Office.

445
00:36:08.000 --> 00:36:12.421
make sure that it was you two
who delivered the Eye. Turn around.

446
00:36:12.504 --> 00:36:16.508
The Eye contains the elixir
from the Pool of Eternal Life.

447
00:36:18.594 --> 00:36:21.388
I need you to open it. Mrs. O'Connell.

448
00:36:22.639 --> 00:36:23.849
No.

449
00:36:24.600 --> 00:36:26.935
You're going to use it to wake the Emperor.
aren't you?

450
00:36:27.019 --> 00:36:31.190
And his Terracotta Army.
At least. that's the general idea.

451
00:36:31.273 --> 00:36:34.818
Raising an army of mummies is insane.
Listen. Yang...

452
00:36:36.445 --> 00:36:38.447
(GRUNTING)

453
00:36:38.530 --> 00:36:40.282
Easy! Go easy.

454
00:36:41.116 --> 00:36:44.244
Time to open the sarcophagus. Move!

455
00:36:48.791 --> 00:36:52.127
Read the inscription! Now!

456
00:37:00.219 --> 00:37:02.930
Ancient Chinese isn't my forte.

457
00:37:03.013 --> 00:37:06.558
Here's some encouragement. Wilson!

458
00:37:07.726 --> 00:37:08.769
I'll do it!

459
00:37:08.852 --> 00:37:12.564
No. Evy. don't do it!
They're just gonna kill me. anyway.

460
00:37:16.568 --> 00:37:19.321
The inscription says
that only a drop of blood

461
00:37:19.405 --> 00:37:22.616
from a person of pure heart
can open the Eye.

462
00:37:24.660 --> 00:37:26.662
Your husband was right.

463
00:37:28.497 --> 00:37:30.040
No!

464
00:37:36.839 --> 00:37:41.385
Only the pure of heart would sacrifice
themselves for the one they love.

465
00:37:42.719 --> 00:37:44.263
Open it.

466
00:37:49.226 --> 00:37:52.146
You never called after our last date.

467
00:37:52.229 --> 00:37:54.565
I don't have time for games. Alex.

468
00:37:54.648 --> 00:37:58.026
You know my name. but I don't know yours.

469
00:37:58.110 --> 00:37:59.319
It's Lin.

470
00:37:59.403 --> 00:38:02.948
You want to explain to me
why you tried to kill me?

471
00:38:03.031 --> 00:38:04.158
We could do that.

472
00:38:04.241 --> 00:38:06.034
Or we could save your parents.

473
00:38:11.039 --> 00:38:13.709
Wilson. you son of a bitch!

474
00:38:27.764 --> 00:38:29.600
(GRUNTING)

475
00:39:06.011 --> 00:39:09.389
- Get on with it. O'Connell.
- All right.

476
00:39:23.820 --> 00:39:24.863
(COUGHS)

477
00:39:28.367 --> 00:39:33.914
Once this touches him.
the Emperor will rise to rule again.

478
00:39:34.998 --> 00:39:36.041
Finish him off.

479
00:39:36.124 --> 00:39:37.167
(GUN COCKING)

480
00:39:54.643 --> 00:39:57.187
(GRUNTING)

481
00:40:15.622 --> 00:40:18.000
Alex. please! Don't. That's...

482
00:40:18.584 --> 00:40:20.836
Don't. don't. Don't. please.

483
00:40:20.919 --> 00:40:23.589
No. don't. Alex. it's me. Please.

484
00:40:24.047 --> 00:40:27.801
It's not him. This is a eunuch! It's a decoy!

485
00:40:29.803 --> 00:40:31.847
Where the hell's the Emperor?

486
00:40:33.056 --> 00:40:35.767
(CLANGING)

487
00:40:58.165 --> 00:40:59.416
Stay!

488
00:41:13.263 --> 00:41:15.724
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

489
00:41:18.268 --> 00:41:19.936
Here we go again.

490
00:41:31.114 --> 00:41:32.157
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

491
00:41:32.240 --> 00:41:34.117
I live to serve you. my Lord.

492
00:41:34.201 --> 00:41:35.786
I can help you become immortal.

493
00:41:35.869 --> 00:41:38.705
If you are lying. you will burn.

494
00:41:55.305 --> 00:41:59.559
Wait! Wait! You wait for me!
I'm coming with you! Wait. wait...

495
00:42:11.988 --> 00:42:15.200
(BOTH GRUNTING)

496
00:42:25.460 --> 00:42:26.837
Watch out!

497
00:42:32.134 --> 00:42:36.054
RICK: We got to put this mummy down fast!
The longer we wait. the stronger they get!

498
00:42:36.138 --> 00:42:38.473
Open the gate! Open the gate!

499
00:42:43.812 --> 00:42:45.731
(SHOUTING IN MANDARIN)

500
00:42:45.814 --> 00:42:49.651
Yeah. yeah. yeah. I know. Sorry. pal.
There's a mummy on the loose.

501
00:42:49.735 --> 00:42:51.027
- You wanna drive?
- Why not?

502
00:42:51.111 --> 00:42:52.904
God. I love a woman who can drive a truck.

503
00:42:52.988 --> 00:42:56.074
Hey. pal. I'm really sorry.
but you know what? Happy New Year!

504
00:42:56.408 --> 00:42:57.701
Hit it. honey!

505
00:43:03.039 --> 00:43:04.750
No! Move over!

506
00:43:06.042 --> 00:43:07.711
What? No!

507
00:43:07.794 --> 00:43:09.129
No!

508
00:43:12.215 --> 00:43:13.258
(SCREAMS)

509
00:43:16.219 --> 00:43:17.554
No!

510
00:43:19.097 --> 00:43:21.641
- What?
- Jonathan. get in the back!

511
00:43:22.976 --> 00:43:24.102
Sorry about the Rolls!

512
00:43:24.186 --> 00:43:26.605
You guys are like mummy magnets!

513
00:43:28.273 --> 00:43:30.859
- We have to turn you around!
- Okay.

514
00:43:36.740 --> 00:43:38.158
Excuse me.

515
00:43:40.619 --> 00:43:43.330
- Hey. we could use this!
- Give me that!

516
00:43:45.665 --> 00:43:49.085
- Oh. yeah. that's a better idea.
- RICK: Size counts!

517
00:43:49.169 --> 00:43:52.088
Stop mucking about! They're getting away!

518
00:43:53.006 --> 00:43:54.758
(GRUNTS) Just drive!

519
00:43:55.425 --> 00:43:57.636
RICK: Aim for the Emperor!
JONATHAN: Aim for the Emperor?

520
00:43:57.719 --> 00:44:00.388
- Light it up. Jonathan!
- I'm trying!

521
00:44:00.472 --> 00:44:01.598
Fire!

522
00:44:01.681 --> 00:44:02.724
(SCREAMS)

523
00:44:12.776 --> 00:44:14.694
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

524
00:44:22.244 --> 00:44:23.745
Did we get him?

525
00:44:23.829 --> 00:44:25.956
- Fire!
- What. again?

526
00:44:26.039 --> 00:44:27.958
- Your ass is on fire!
- My ass?

527
00:44:28.041 --> 00:44:29.918
- Hold still!
- Rick. my ass is on fire!

528
00:44:30.001 --> 00:44:31.461
- Well. spank my...
- I'm putting it out!

529
00:44:31.545 --> 00:44:33.296
- Put me out. Rick!
- Just hold still!

530
00:44:33.380 --> 00:44:35.674
Spank my ass! Spank my ass!

531
00:44:35.757 --> 00:44:37.717
All right. here I come!

532
00:44:40.679 --> 00:44:42.472
LIN: Give me your hand!

533
00:44:48.687 --> 00:44:49.729
Come on!

534
00:44:50.313 --> 00:44:51.731
Watch out!

535
00:44:52.649 --> 00:44:53.775
RICK: Evy. where are you going?

536
00:44:53.859 --> 00:44:55.986
- Taking a short cut!
- Evy!

537
00:44:56.361 --> 00:44:58.488
(BOTH SCREAMING)

538
00:45:05.453 --> 00:45:07.497
- I told you it was a short cut!
- Right!

539
00:45:07.581 --> 00:45:09.457
Now he's chasing us!

540
00:45:10.500 --> 00:45:11.543
(YELPS)

541
00:45:12.836 --> 00:45:13.879
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

542
00:45:13.962 --> 00:45:15.213
Hurry!

543
00:45:16.381 --> 00:45:19.050
Give me your hand.
Here. you're gonna need these.

544
00:45:19.134 --> 00:45:21.011
- Don't wait up for me.
- Where are you going?

545
00:45:21.094 --> 00:45:22.220
Out!

546
00:45:28.351 --> 00:45:31.021
- Where's Rick?
- Where do you think?

547
00:45:37.235 --> 00:45:38.612
Damn it!

548
00:45:42.741 --> 00:45:44.242
You're mine!

549
00:45:44.326 --> 00:45:46.661
(HORSES NEIGHING)

550
00:45:49.414 --> 00:45:53.043
- Give me your hand and get on this horse!
- Get back. Dad!

551
00:45:53.126 --> 00:45:58.089
Alexander Rupert O'Connell. you get
on the back of this horse this instant!

552
00:46:04.596 --> 00:46:07.390
(EXCLAIMING)

553
00:46:07.474 --> 00:46:11.645
Get out of the way! Get out of the way!
Oh. God!

554
00:46:17.734 --> 00:46:18.818
(SCREAMING)

555
00:46:18.902 --> 00:46:20.070
JONATHAN: Evy!

556
00:46:21.154 --> 00:46:22.739
We've got to go back and help Rick!

557
00:46:22.822 --> 00:46:25.700
JONATHAN: Rick! Forget Rick!
Here they come!

558
00:46:34.250 --> 00:46:35.919
I'll go after the Emperor.

559
00:46:36.002 --> 00:46:38.755
Trust me. I've got a little more experience
with mummies.

560
00:46:38.838 --> 00:46:42.342
And I have the only weapon
that can kill him.

561
00:46:42.425 --> 00:46:44.844
Okay. I'll cover you. Let's go!

562
00:46:53.186 --> 00:46:54.354
ALEX: Lin!

563
00:46:55.855 --> 00:46:56.898
(SCREAMS)

564
00:47:12.080 --> 00:47:14.791
- I thought you were dead!
- He missed.

565
00:47:26.553 --> 00:47:29.848
(EXCLAIMING)

566
00:47:41.776 --> 00:47:43.194
LIN: Look out!

567
00:48:24.402 --> 00:48:26.988
(PANTING)

568
00:48:29.449 --> 00:48:33.995
- Thanks. Rick. Could you get the cab?
- Does it look like I have a wallet?

569
00:48:53.014 --> 00:48:55.767
You know. I would have killed the Emperor
if you two hadn't blown my cover.

570
00:48:55.850 --> 00:48:57.102
I had everything under control.

571
00:48:57.185 --> 00:48:59.437
Oh. yeah. that's exactly
what we were thinking.

572
00:48:59.521 --> 00:49:01.356
Yeah. well. good going.
you raised another mummy.

573
00:49:01.439 --> 00:49:03.399
And this bugger's got superpowers.

574
00:49:03.483 --> 00:49:06.736
ALEX: He's got control over fire. water.
metal and who knows what else.

575
00:49:06.820 --> 00:49:07.904
And you dug him up anyway.

576
00:49:07.987 --> 00:49:09.739
Yeah. well. you're not gonna
pin this one on me. okay. Dad?

577
00:49:09.823 --> 00:49:12.075
- RICK: Am I?
- Oh. stop it. you two.

578
00:49:12.158 --> 00:49:15.578
No one's to blame here.
Wilson manipulated all of us.

579
00:49:15.662 --> 00:49:16.788
Yeah. that's true.

580
00:49:16.871 --> 00:49:18.957
I apologize for my parents.

581
00:49:19.040 --> 00:49:21.876
But I thought we worked
really well together.

582
00:49:22.377 --> 00:49:24.129
Except we failed.

583
00:49:26.339 --> 00:49:29.634
I'm sorry.
we haven't been properly introduced.

584
00:49:29.717 --> 00:49:32.303
- Who are you exactly?
- My name is Lin.

585
00:49:32.387 --> 00:49:35.765
My family has watched
over the Emperor's tomb for centuries.

586
00:49:35.849 --> 00:49:40.186
The Emperor cannot be killed unless
he is stabbed through the heart with this.

587
00:49:40.270 --> 00:49:42.981
My mother put a curse on it long ago.

588
00:49:44.357 --> 00:49:45.400
Mmm-hmm.

589
00:49:46.359 --> 00:49:48.987
Well. a quick family meeting. Alex.

590
00:49:50.738 --> 00:49:52.282
- Sit.
- Down.

591
00:49:54.325 --> 00:49:56.327
What do you really know about this girl?

592
00:49:56.411 --> 00:50:01.166
Well. not much. but after her help tonight.
I'm willing to go on a little faith.

593
00:50:01.249 --> 00:50:03.126
- Faith.
- Time is running out.

594
00:50:03.209 --> 00:50:05.712
You don't really believe in the concept
of personal space. do you?

595
00:50:05.795 --> 00:50:09.299
If the Emperor reaches Shangri-La
and drinks from the Pool of Eternal Life.

596
00:50:09.382 --> 00:50:12.260
he will raise his army
and no one will be safe.

597
00:50:12.343 --> 00:50:14.888
Much as I'd like to stay
this boyishly handsome forever.

598
00:50:14.971 --> 00:50:16.431
Shangri-La is a crock.

599
00:50:16.514 --> 00:50:18.474
Yeah. but that's what you used to say
about mummies. too. Jon.

600
00:50:18.558 --> 00:50:20.685
- You did pretty well off it.
- Good point.

601
00:50:20.768 --> 00:50:25.190
The Gateway to Shangri-La lies in
a mountain pass high in the Himalayas.

602
00:50:25.273 --> 00:50:27.442
Beyond it is a golden tower.

603
00:50:27.525 --> 00:50:31.237
Once the diamond is placed at the top.
it will point the way to Shangri-La.

604
00:50:31.321 --> 00:50:33.364
Yang still has the diamond.

605
00:50:33.448 --> 00:50:36.451
and that's where
he and the Emperor will go.

606
00:50:36.993 --> 00:50:38.036
She's right.

607
00:50:38.119 --> 00:50:41.206
All the legends of the Eye
mention the Gateway.

608
00:50:41.289 --> 00:50:43.458
I like her. Alex. She knows what's what.

609
00:50:43.541 --> 00:50:49.047
Now. just say that we were to believe you.
could you guide us there?

610
00:50:49.130 --> 00:50:52.550
Yes. I have been there once.
I remember the way.

611
00:50:55.386 --> 00:50:57.847
Himalayas. We're going to need a plane.

612
00:50:57.931 --> 00:51:00.725
Well. I know just the Mad Dog for the job.

613
00:51:04.103 --> 00:51:07.023
MAGUIRE: Well. any self-respecting pilot
would land on the valley floor.

614
00:51:07.106 --> 00:51:08.858
but I don't have any self-respect.

615
00:51:08.942 --> 00:51:11.194
so I'll put you down
halfway up the mountain.

616
00:51:11.277 --> 00:51:13.029
That should give us a good advantage.

617
00:51:13.112 --> 00:51:15.198
MAGUIRE: Of course.
I can't guarantee any of us will live.

618
00:51:15.281 --> 00:51:16.491
Great!

619
00:51:20.245 --> 00:51:24.123
I'd tell you to fasten your seat belts.
but I was too cheap to buy any!

620
00:51:24.207 --> 00:51:26.417
(LAUGHING)

621
00:51:26.918 --> 00:51:29.295
- Why am I laughing?
- Here we go!

622
00:51:30.255 --> 00:51:33.508
RICK: Mad Dog. Mad Dog!
Ease up. ease up. ease up!

623
00:51:33.883 --> 00:51:35.343
JONATHAN: Oh. God!

624
00:51:37.929 --> 00:51:40.473
(SCREAMING)

625
00:51:43.101 --> 00:51:44.852
JONATHAN: Maguire!

626
00:51:46.521 --> 00:51:48.106
Come on. man!

627
00:51:48.564 --> 00:51:49.816
Mad Dog!

628
00:51:57.407 --> 00:51:59.117
(YAK BELLOWING)

629
00:52:02.287 --> 00:52:03.955
RICK: Brake! No. no! Nobody move.

630
00:52:04.038 --> 00:52:06.791
Nobody move. nobody move!

631
00:52:20.221 --> 00:52:22.473
What is that God-awful smell?

632
00:52:23.808 --> 00:52:25.476
The yak yakked.

633
00:52:28.771 --> 00:52:29.814
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

634
00:52:29.897 --> 00:52:32.233
Welcome to the modern world. my Lord.

635
00:52:32.775 --> 00:52:34.694
Why did you raise me?

636
00:52:35.111 --> 00:52:39.324
I love this land.
Only you can lead us back to greatness.

637
00:52:40.199 --> 00:52:42.577
What is in it for you?

638
00:52:44.162 --> 00:52:46.956
I want to serve as your general.

639
00:52:47.665 --> 00:52:50.126
The last general I trusted...

640
00:52:50.418 --> 00:52:53.212
betrayed me.

641
00:52:53.796 --> 00:52:56.549
I will not make that mistake.

642
00:53:02.972 --> 00:53:07.518
I cannot escape this curse
until I am immortal...

643
00:53:08.311 --> 00:53:09.812
General.

644
00:53:11.522 --> 00:53:13.524
I understand. my Lord.

645
00:53:13.816 --> 00:53:17.695
We need to find the Pool of Eternal Life.

646
00:53:18.571 --> 00:53:22.450
This will point the way.

647
00:53:24.619 --> 00:53:27.538
(ROARS)

648
00:53:43.888 --> 00:53:45.640
(MAGUIRE SINGING)
<i>Can't you see it's Mr. McGuire</i>

649
00:53:45.723 --> 00:53:47.558
<i>come to court your sister Kate</i>

650
00:53:47.642 --> 00:53:51.729
<i>You know very well he owns the farm
a wee bit out...</i>

651
00:53:51.813 --> 00:53:53.648
(PLANE ENGINE HUMMING)

652
00:54:04.075 --> 00:54:07.245
<i>MAGUIRE OVER RADIO: Delta-Tango-Alpha
to Ricochet. Come in. Ricochet.</i>

653
00:54:09.247 --> 00:54:11.749
Delta-Tango-Alpha. this is Ricochet.
Go ahead. Mad Dog.

654
00:54:11.833 --> 00:54:14.293
Yeah. you know that Yang fellow
you told me to keep me eye out for?

655
00:54:14.377 --> 00:54:15.586
<i>He's just shown up.</i>

656
00:54:15.670 --> 00:54:17.922
Ricochet out. Thanks. Mad Dog.

657
00:54:18.005 --> 00:54:19.674
That's us. people! Let's go!

658
00:54:19.757 --> 00:54:21.592
- Jonathan. wake up!
- What...

659
00:54:31.352 --> 00:54:32.937
Hold the line!

660
00:54:36.441 --> 00:54:37.608
Good. we're a little more than halfway.

661
00:54:37.692 --> 00:54:41.237
We're gonna...
We're gonna camp up there for the night.

662
00:54:54.000 --> 00:54:58.254
ALEX: Lin says if we leave at first light.
we'll reach the Gateway by noon.

663
00:54:59.797 --> 00:55:03.759
Did she happen to mention how she knows
so much about the Gateway?

664
00:55:03.843 --> 00:55:06.637
No. not really. Kind of mysterious.

665
00:55:07.430 --> 00:55:10.183
She's certainly managed to enchant you.

666
00:55:12.351 --> 00:55:15.021
Come on. Alex. You obviously like her.

667
00:55:16.939 --> 00:55:20.568
Mom. the thin mountain air.
clearly messing with your head.

668
00:55:22.445 --> 00:55:24.655
Whatever secret she's hiding.

669
00:55:25.907 --> 00:55:28.034
I just don't want to see you get hurt.

670
00:55:28.117 --> 00:55:31.579
I appreciate that. but. you know.

671
00:55:31.662 --> 00:55:35.708
I've had my fair share of experience
with the opposite sex.

672
00:55:35.791 --> 00:55:36.959
Really?

673
00:55:38.711 --> 00:55:41.506
How many experiences
are we talking about?

674
00:55:42.798 --> 00:55:48.012
Well. you shouldn't ask questions you don't
want to know the answer to. okay. Mom?

675
00:55:48.095 --> 00:55:49.222
Right.

676
00:55:50.348 --> 00:55:52.225
Hey. Mom.

677
00:55:54.227 --> 00:55:57.855
I'm sorry I blamed you guys
for raising the Emperor.

678
00:56:09.033 --> 00:56:10.701
What's so funny?

679
00:56:13.913 --> 00:56:18.292
My mother is under the impression
there's something between us.

680
00:56:18.376 --> 00:56:20.378
I hope nothing romantic.

681
00:56:23.381 --> 00:56:26.968
Yeah. well. I told her there
was no chance of that.

682
00:56:27.051 --> 00:56:29.428
We're complete opposites.
you and me. right?

683
00:56:29.512 --> 00:56:34.559
You guard tombs. I raid them.
You like ancient knives. I'm into guns.

684
00:56:35.268 --> 00:56:37.728
Those are some
pretty insurmountable odds.

685
00:56:37.812 --> 00:56:40.064
- Absolutely.
- Well. good.

686
00:56:40.940 --> 00:56:45.152
Now that we've cleared that up.
we can focus on taking down the Emperor.

687
00:56:45.236 --> 00:56:46.862
I agree totally.

688
00:56:49.490 --> 00:56:52.201
Besides. you're not my type.

689
00:56:55.162 --> 00:56:59.292
Of course not. You don't like a woman
who can knock you on your backside.

690
00:56:59.375 --> 00:57:01.502
(CHUCKLES)

691
00:57:01.586 --> 00:57:04.005
The expression is "kick my ass."

692
00:57:05.006 --> 00:57:07.508
And for the record. you didn't.

693
00:57:10.219 --> 00:57:13.472
Yeah. it's not easy being me. you know.

694
00:57:13.556 --> 00:57:15.266
Then again. I don't suppose
it's easy being you.

695
00:57:15.349 --> 00:57:17.518
is it. Geraldine. old girl?

696
00:57:17.602 --> 00:57:19.812
If I'd met a girl like you. Geraldine...

697
00:57:19.895 --> 00:57:22.815
You know. hard-working.
you don't say much.

698
00:57:23.858 --> 00:57:27.278
you're a little bit hairy. but I don't mind that.

699
00:57:38.372 --> 00:57:40.625
There it is! We found it!

700
00:57:48.591 --> 00:57:50.635
The Gateway of Shangri-La!

701
00:57:58.142 --> 00:58:02.104
JONATHAN: Go. girl! Go! You're free!

702
00:58:02.188 --> 00:58:05.399
Go. Geraldine! Live free!

703
00:58:15.576 --> 00:58:18.287
What did you do now? Rob an armory?

704
00:58:19.455 --> 00:58:21.832
Have you ever seen a Walther P38?

705
00:58:21.916 --> 00:58:24.168
Looks pretty anemic
compared to the Peacekeeper.

706
00:58:24.251 --> 00:58:27.630
Well. it's not about size. Dad.
It's about stamina.

707
00:58:30.132 --> 00:58:31.676
You want power?

708
00:58:33.094 --> 00:58:38.182
I give you the Thompson submachine gun.
Fifty rounds a drum.

709
00:58:38.265 --> 00:58:41.435
- Twenty-five a mag.
- Tommy's good. Dad.

710
00:58:41.519 --> 00:58:43.229
but the cocking mechanism always jams.

711
00:58:43.312 --> 00:58:47.692
Here. Check out the Russian PPS
Personal Assault Weapon.

712
00:58:47.775 --> 00:58:49.485
Now. this is the future right here.

713
00:58:49.610 --> 00:58:52.947
You know. it's experience that wins the day.
It's not all about firepower.

714
00:58:53.030 --> 00:58:54.990
Boys! If I may...

715
00:58:55.116 --> 00:58:56.951
Do we have a plan for the Emperor?

716
00:58:57.034 --> 00:58:58.994
Yeah. We're gonna hit him
high. hard and fast

717
00:58:59.120 --> 00:59:00.830
and smash him like a Ming vase.

718
00:59:00.955 --> 00:59:04.041
- And if that doesn't work?
- We go to plan B.

719
00:59:04.125 --> 00:59:07.294
Plan B! You go upstairs.
you blow up that gold tower thing.

720
00:59:07.378 --> 00:59:09.505
- You light it up. We blow the guy sky high!
- Me?

721
00:59:09.630 --> 00:59:10.631
- You! What?
- Dad?

722
00:59:10.715 --> 00:59:12.842
So if the explosion doesn't kill us.
the avalanche will.

723
00:59:12.967 --> 00:59:14.427
- You got a better idea?
- Yeah. I do.

724
00:59:14.510 --> 00:59:16.387
I say we ambush him
with long-range rifles and silencers.

725
00:59:16.470 --> 00:59:17.555
Long-range. that's a better idea.

726
00:59:17.638 --> 00:59:18.723
Yeah. we can get in close. Dad.

727
00:59:18.806 --> 00:59:19.932
- JONATHAN: Much better idea.
- And then we can finish him off

728
00:59:20.015 --> 00:59:21.642
- with Lin's dagger.
- Look. I'm sorry.

729
00:59:21.726 --> 00:59:24.395
I just don't put much faith
in your girlfriend's magic dagger.

730
00:59:24.478 --> 00:59:26.689
- Okay. Dad. she is not my girlfriend.
- You say that now.

731
00:59:26.814 --> 00:59:28.858
- but I still don't trust her.
- Well. I do.

732
00:59:28.983 --> 00:59:31.652
- So you should trust my judgment. okay?
- Look. kid.

733
00:59:31.736 --> 00:59:33.404
I've put down more mummies
in my time than you.

734
00:59:33.487 --> 00:59:34.905
You put down one mummy. Dad.

735
00:59:34.989 --> 00:59:38.200
Yeah. Same mummy twice!

736
00:59:42.705 --> 00:59:45.499
EVELYN: Hand me the green wire.
will you. please?

737
00:59:46.500 --> 00:59:48.419
Are you sure you know what you are doing?

738
00:59:48.502 --> 00:59:50.671
Of course. I've done this a hundred times.

739
00:59:50.755 --> 00:59:54.341
If the Emperor places the Eye up there.
all will be lost.

740
00:59:58.846 --> 01:00:00.848
(PANTING)

741
01:00:07.062 --> 01:00:08.105
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

742
01:00:08.189 --> 01:00:09.940
Clear a path to the Golden Tower.

743
01:00:10.524 --> 01:00:13.527
Prove yourself to me.

744
01:00:19.784 --> 01:00:20.868
(ORDERING TROOPS)

745
01:00:27.708 --> 01:00:29.460
Let's give a warm O'Connell welcome!

746
01:00:31.253 --> 01:00:32.880
(COMMANDING)

747
01:00:33.756 --> 01:00:34.924
Fire!

748
01:00:35.090 --> 01:00:36.759
(MACHINE GUN FIRING)

749
01:00:38.761 --> 01:00:41.555
(SCREAMING)

750
01:00:48.062 --> 01:00:49.313
Bazooka!

751
01:00:54.485 --> 01:00:55.903
RICK: Fall back!

752
01:01:05.246 --> 01:01:07.623
Alex! Follow me!

753
01:01:18.968 --> 01:01:21.095
(ORDERING IN MANDARIN)

754
01:01:22.972 --> 01:01:24.765
We gotta take out those bazookas!

755
01:01:26.767 --> 01:01:27.977
Go!

756
01:01:36.026 --> 01:01:37.444
Fall back!

757
01:01:37.945 --> 01:01:40.030
Move! Move! Move! Move!

758
01:01:47.538 --> 01:01:49.999
Time to go to plan B! Blow up the tower!

759
01:01:50.124 --> 01:01:51.959
Hey. I'm actually a little bit concerned
about plan B!

760
01:01:52.042 --> 01:01:53.460
Couldn't we go straight to plan C?

761
01:01:53.544 --> 01:01:56.171
Just make it go bang! I'll cover you!

762
01:01:57.339 --> 01:01:58.632
Come on.

763
01:01:59.466 --> 01:02:01.719
All right. let's go. go. go!
Come on. come on!

764
01:02:01.802 --> 01:02:03.637
Come on. Oh. be good.

765
01:02:22.323 --> 01:02:23.365
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

766
01:02:23.490 --> 01:02:24.992
Set up a crossfire!

767
01:02:25.659 --> 01:02:26.952
Move it!

768
01:02:30.664 --> 01:02:32.041
(GUN CLICKING)

769
01:02:35.336 --> 01:02:37.004
EVELYN: My last round!

770
01:02:41.216 --> 01:02:45.512
(SHOUTING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

771
01:03:00.694 --> 01:03:04.865
- Abominable snowmen?
- The Tibetans call them yeti!

772
01:03:06.241 --> 01:03:07.409
(SNARLS)

773
01:03:07.868 --> 01:03:08.911
(SPEAKING FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

774
01:03:09.036 --> 01:03:10.412
Please! I need your help!

775
01:03:10.704 --> 01:03:12.706
These soldiers are evil!

776
01:03:14.875 --> 01:03:16.669
She speaks Yeti?

777
01:03:25.344 --> 01:03:27.054
(YETI ROARS)

778
01:03:32.059 --> 01:03:33.143
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

779
01:03:33.227 --> 01:03:34.895
Shoot! Kill them!

780
01:03:42.736 --> 01:03:45.572
Why do I always have to save the day?

781
01:03:46.198 --> 01:03:47.533
I hate it when the kid's right!

782
01:03:47.950 --> 01:03:49.910
(GRUNTING)

783
01:03:51.745 --> 01:03:53.414
Get the other guy!

784
01:03:54.415 --> 01:03:55.582
Thanks!

785
01:04:20.941 --> 01:04:22.276
Trouble!

786
01:04:32.953 --> 01:04:35.289
(SCREAMING)

787
01:04:38.333 --> 01:04:41.253
(ROARING)

788
01:04:45.132 --> 01:04:48.635
(GRUNTING)

789
01:05:01.815 --> 01:05:04.359
You can die slow or you can die fast.

790
01:05:11.158 --> 01:05:12.659
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

791
01:05:17.539 --> 01:05:19.458
(GRUNTING)

792
01:05:26.465 --> 01:05:28.842
Yes! Yes! Yes!

793
01:05:30.177 --> 01:05:32.679
(LAUGHING TRIUMPHANTLY)
Yeah! I did it!

794
01:05:33.347 --> 01:05:37.684
Oh. Mother. I did it!
Time for a retreat. I think.

795
01:05:42.856 --> 01:05:47.861
I'm on your team! I'm a team player!
"One for all and all for me" kind of thing!

796
01:05:48.862 --> 01:05:52.366
The dynamite. all this dynamite!
We should get out of here!

797
01:06:08.215 --> 01:06:09.716
Back off! Back off!

798
01:06:10.050 --> 01:06:11.635
LIN: Run!

799
01:06:20.894 --> 01:06:22.813
(ROARING)

800
01:06:39.413 --> 01:06:43.041
(GROANS) I hate mummies!
They never play fair!

801
01:06:51.091 --> 01:06:53.427
Dad! Dad. what are you doing?

802
01:07:01.101 --> 01:07:04.730
Over here! Over here! Come on! Over here!

803
01:07:05.522 --> 01:07:06.899
Oh. no!

804
01:07:12.529 --> 01:07:13.614
Rick!

805
01:07:16.575 --> 01:07:18.452
(SCREAMING)

806
01:07:40.933 --> 01:07:41.975
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

807
01:07:42.059 --> 01:07:43.977
Shangri-La.

808
01:07:52.736 --> 01:07:54.446
That's a diamond.

809
01:07:56.949 --> 01:07:58.492
I could use a diamond like that.

810
01:08:21.181 --> 01:08:22.516
Dad!

811
01:08:26.019 --> 01:08:27.354
(JONATHAN SCREAMS)

812
01:08:29.439 --> 01:08:31.942
Okay. hold it. Hold on there. Dad.

813
01:08:32.025 --> 01:08:35.195
All right. please. please. please
put pressure on it. okay. Dad?

814
01:08:35.279 --> 01:08:38.615
RICK: It's all right. it's all right.
We've been in tougher scrapes than this.

815
01:08:45.163 --> 01:08:46.790
Avalanche!

816
01:08:54.631 --> 01:08:57.843
(EMPEROR ROARING)

817
01:09:11.231 --> 01:09:12.232
(LIN GASPS)

818
01:09:19.364 --> 01:09:21.533
- Help! Help me!
- Lin!

819
01:09:26.580 --> 01:09:28.081
Please! Help me!

820
01:09:38.258 --> 01:09:40.385
(SCREAMING)

821
01:10:00.405 --> 01:10:01.865
(CRUNCHING)

822
01:10:04.368 --> 01:10:07.371
(YETI GROWLING)

823
01:10:09.831 --> 01:10:11.208
Yes!

824
01:10:11.291 --> 01:10:12.459
(LAUGHING HYSTERICALLY)

825
01:10:12.542 --> 01:10:15.087
I've got it! And I'm still alive!

826
01:10:18.965 --> 01:10:21.510
ALEX: (MUFFLED) Help me. please.
Somebody help me!

827
01:10:22.260 --> 01:10:25.097
- We're over here! Over here!
- Alex?

828
01:10:25.180 --> 01:10:27.766
- ALEX:Mom. Mom. we're down here!
- Alex?

829
01:10:28.100 --> 01:10:29.559
We're over here!

830
01:10:29.643 --> 01:10:31.395
(ALEX PANTING)

831
01:10:41.947 --> 01:10:43.240
Oh. God.

832
01:10:44.658 --> 01:10:48.537
We've got to take him to Shangri-La now!
It's our only chance.

833
01:11:08.098 --> 01:11:09.474
We made it!

834
01:11:27.367 --> 01:11:28.785
The Pool.

835
01:11:38.712 --> 01:11:39.796
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

836
01:11:39.880 --> 01:11:41.047
Mother.

837
01:11:42.549 --> 01:11:43.592
My sweet daughter.

838
01:11:52.476 --> 01:11:53.560
I beg you...

839
01:11:55.312 --> 01:11:57.189
My father is dying.

840
01:11:57.647 --> 01:11:58.940
They are my friends.

841
01:11:59.941 --> 01:12:01.318
Oh. please.

842
01:12:01.693 --> 01:12:02.736
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

843
01:12:19.669 --> 01:12:21.004
(RICK GASPS)

844
01:12:37.646 --> 01:12:39.022
Thank you.

845
01:12:40.440 --> 01:12:43.485
He must rest. We'll take him to my chamber.

846
01:13:00.335 --> 01:13:01.378
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

847
01:13:01.461 --> 01:13:05.006
Where are you going. General?
Our destiny awaits.

848
01:13:10.178 --> 01:13:14.891
Well. it's not everyone that gets
their brother-in-law back from the dead.

849
01:13:15.517 --> 01:13:18.853
Yeah. give me my four score years
and ten any day.

850
01:13:23.858 --> 01:13:25.735
Is this Shangri-La?

851
01:13:35.704 --> 01:13:38.540
I could live here. Lots of opportunity.

852
01:13:40.542 --> 01:13:42.002
A casino.

853
01:13:45.797 --> 01:13:46.840
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

854
01:13:46.923 --> 01:13:50.260
I was wrong to involve you in my revenge.

855
01:13:50.802 --> 01:13:52.304
No. mother.

856
01:13:53.388 --> 01:13:55.557
I would do anything for you.

857
01:14:04.858 --> 01:14:07.235
ALEX: He's resting well. Thank you.

858
01:14:08.987 --> 01:14:11.406
How'd you get involved in all this?

859
01:14:11.489 --> 01:14:16.536
The Emperor murdered the only man
I ever loved. Lin's father.

860
01:14:18.038 --> 01:14:20.874
I would have died. too. by his hand.

861
01:14:20.957 --> 01:14:24.878
if the yeti had not found me
and brought me to this pool.

862
01:14:24.961 --> 01:14:28.048
Hang on a second.
How did this all happen?

863
01:14:28.131 --> 01:14:30.091
This was before Christ.

864
01:14:33.053 --> 01:14:35.847
How long were you guarding his tomb?

865
01:14:35.930 --> 01:14:37.599
Over 2.000 years.

866
01:14:43.772 --> 01:14:46.066
The Emperor must never be
allowed to reach the Pool.

867
01:14:46.149 --> 01:14:49.069
or he will have the power to raise his army.

868
01:14:49.152 --> 01:14:50.779
And once he becomes immortal.

869
01:14:50.862 --> 01:14:54.908
he can transform himself into
the most hideous creatures ever seen.

870
01:14:54.991 --> 01:14:57.952
I will take the first watch at the entrance.

871
01:15:04.668 --> 01:15:08.213
You know. I have no problem
dating an older woman.

872
01:15:11.091 --> 01:15:13.426
I'm afraid we can't be together.

873
01:15:14.344 --> 01:15:16.930
Wait. What? Why?

874
01:15:18.640 --> 01:15:21.184
Because I'm going to live forever.

875
01:15:21.935 --> 01:15:24.270
I don't want to watch you die.

876
01:15:25.188 --> 01:15:27.065
So what? That's it?

877
01:15:28.024 --> 01:15:31.069
You're just gonna sit
on the sidelines for eternity?

878
01:15:31.152 --> 01:15:34.239
My mother has mourned
my father for centuries.

879
01:15:34.823 --> 01:15:37.534
I don't know if my heart can bear it.

880
01:15:42.205 --> 01:15:45.375
People can live an entire lifetime
in one look.

881
01:15:47.585 --> 01:15:50.088
I watch my parents do it every day.

882
01:15:53.174 --> 01:15:54.217
JONATHAN: Alex?

883
01:15:54.217 --> 01:15:54.342
JONATHAN: Alex?

884
01:15:55.719 --> 01:15:58.304
Your father's awake. Get up here!

885
01:16:11.151 --> 01:16:12.402
Hello.

886
01:16:15.280 --> 01:16:18.450
If this is heaven. it looks pretty good so far.

887
01:16:26.666 --> 01:16:29.252
Nice to see some things never change.

888
01:16:47.353 --> 01:16:49.856
Go easy on him. He feels terrible.

889
01:16:55.528 --> 01:16:58.031
When I saw you lying there. Dad...

890
01:16:58.364 --> 01:17:01.242
I've never been so scared in my life.

891
01:17:02.827 --> 01:17:05.079
Well. that makes two of us.

892
01:17:06.122 --> 01:17:09.083
I mean. you know.
you're not supposed to die. you know?

893
01:17:09.167 --> 01:17:11.211
You're Ricochet O'Connell. right?

894
01:17:11.294 --> 01:17:14.547
You get beat up. you get tossed around.

895
01:17:14.631 --> 01:17:17.258
but. well. you're always standing there
in the end.

896
01:17:17.342 --> 01:17:20.553
I never really thought of
the world without you.

897
01:17:24.224 --> 01:17:25.683
Alex.

898
01:17:27.644 --> 01:17:29.395
the truth is.

899
01:17:31.856 --> 01:17:33.608
I'm just trying to...

900
01:17:35.693 --> 01:17:37.654
I'm just...

901
01:17:37.737 --> 01:17:38.947
I'm trying to be a good husband.

902
01:17:39.072 --> 01:17:40.406
I'm trying to be a good parent.

903
01:17:40.490 --> 01:17:44.077
And the truth is.
I've been dropping the ball lately. and...

904
01:17:44.160 --> 01:17:47.121
No. you know. I haven't been
the world's greatest son. you know?

905
01:17:47.247 --> 01:17:51.251
No. no. that's 'cause you get it
from her side of the family.

906
01:17:51.334 --> 01:17:52.752
Come here.

907
01:17:56.422 --> 01:17:57.757
My boys.

908
01:18:01.135 --> 01:18:02.220
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

909
01:18:02.303 --> 01:18:05.139
You look tired. you should rest.

910
01:18:06.140 --> 01:18:07.308
I'll stay.

911
01:18:08.476 --> 01:18:10.645
Fate is about to deal its final hand.

912
01:18:10.979 --> 01:18:13.273
If we are to defeat the Emperor...

913
01:18:13.606 --> 01:18:17.193
I must ask for one more sacrifice.

914
01:18:17.610 --> 01:18:18.862
Anything. mother.

915
01:18:20.780 --> 01:18:22.866
Your immortality.

916
01:18:26.327 --> 01:18:27.370
(EXPLOSION)

917
01:18:34.836 --> 01:18:37.463
Oh. no! His powers have been fully restored!

918
01:18:37.547 --> 01:18:38.882
Time to go.

919
01:19:01.362 --> 01:19:02.405
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

920
01:19:02.488 --> 01:19:04.866
General Ming's daughter.

921
01:19:05.700 --> 01:19:08.036
Your child will be mine.

922
01:19:16.836 --> 01:19:18.838
He is immortal.

923
01:19:47.533 --> 01:19:50.787
Hey! You three-headed shape-shifting
son of a bitch!

924
01:19:59.545 --> 01:20:01.422
(LIN GRUNTING)

925
01:20:01.547 --> 01:20:02.548
Lin!

926
01:20:13.559 --> 01:20:14.769
LIN: Alex!

927
01:20:18.398 --> 01:20:19.482
Alex!

928
01:20:28.658 --> 01:20:30.868
He's taking her back to his tomb
to raise his army!

929
01:20:30.952 --> 01:20:34.080
- Is there a faster way down from here?
- The yeti. They'll help.

930
01:20:34.163 --> 01:20:36.249
But he's already in the air. It'll be too late!

931
01:20:36.332 --> 01:20:40.503
Mad Dog can out fly a three-headed lizard
any day of the week! Let's go.

932
01:20:45.925 --> 01:20:47.802
MAGUIRE: Portside! Nine o'clock!

933
01:20:55.018 --> 01:20:57.687
Rick? Should I quit drinking?

934
01:21:03.609 --> 01:21:04.610
<i>OVER RADIO: Jonathan to Rick.</i>

935
01:21:04.694 --> 01:21:06.696
<i>You'd better get a move on if
you're gonna beat him to the tomb!</i>

936
01:21:06.779 --> 01:21:09.490
RICK: Yeah. yeah. just get back here as fast
as you can with the reinforcements.

937
01:21:09.615 --> 01:21:11.325
No sightseeing!

938
01:21:13.870 --> 01:21:15.621
Here. Dad.

939
01:21:15.705 --> 01:21:16.748
- Is that for me?
- Yeah.

940
01:21:16.831 --> 01:21:17.999
Nice.

941
01:21:18.791 --> 01:21:22.795
The Terracotta Army is not indestructible
until it crosses the Great Wall.

942
01:21:22.879 --> 01:21:26.257
That's comforting. How exactly are we
supposed to fend them off?

943
01:21:26.340 --> 01:21:27.592
When the Emperor built the Wall.

944
01:21:27.675 --> 01:21:29.052
he buried his enemies underneath it

945
01:21:29.135 --> 01:21:31.554
and cursed their souls
to hold it up for eternity.

946
01:21:31.637 --> 01:21:36.559
Most of them were conquered soldiers.
I will call them to battle once again.

947
01:21:36.642 --> 01:21:42.148
Unlock an altar. raise an army.
That sounds like a plan. Let's go.

948
01:21:51.991 --> 01:21:54.494
(SOLDIERS SHOUTING)

949
01:22:08.007 --> 01:22:09.008
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

950
01:22:09.133 --> 01:22:10.301
Grab her.

951
01:22:11.010 --> 01:22:12.678
Guard her with your life.

952
01:22:15.807 --> 01:22:17.016
Alex?

953
01:22:19.310 --> 01:22:21.854
- Where'd he go?
- Where do you think?

954
01:22:38.538 --> 01:22:39.539
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

955
01:22:39.664 --> 01:22:41.249
AWAKE!

956
01:23:27.211 --> 01:23:28.754
(HORSE NEIGHING)

957
01:24:17.470 --> 01:24:19.639
Today you awake to a world...

958
01:24:20.348 --> 01:24:22.725
in the grip of chaos and corruption.

959
01:24:22.808 --> 01:24:24.894
Open the gates of the past

960
01:24:24.977 --> 01:24:27.521
and free the souls
of the wrongfully damned.

961
01:24:28.272 --> 01:24:30.149
I will restore order...

962
01:24:30.816 --> 01:24:33.152
I will retake what is mine.

963
01:24:33.819 --> 01:24:36.489
I will crush any idea of freedom.

964
01:24:36.614 --> 01:24:39.700
In the name of the ancestors
and the righteous.

965
01:24:39.825 --> 01:24:43.162
I sacrifice my immortality
and that of my daughter

966
01:24:43.287 --> 01:24:45.164
so that you may rise this day!

967
01:24:45.289 --> 01:24:47.166
I will slaughter without mercy.

968
01:24:47.500 --> 01:24:50.002
I will conquer without compassion.

969
01:24:50.336 --> 01:24:52.672
I will now lead you past the Great Wall.

970
01:24:53.005 --> 01:24:56.634
Once you cross. you will be indestructible.

971
01:24:57.551 --> 01:25:02.723
Bring down the wrath of the oppressed
on this Emperor and all who follow him!

972
01:25:03.224 --> 01:25:05.351
I raised you for one purpose...

973
01:25:05.685 --> 01:25:08.396
to enforce my will on the entire world!

974
01:25:09.063 --> 01:25:10.523
Long live the Emperor!

975
01:25:13.150 --> 01:25:16.487
I call upon the hundreds and the thousands

976
01:25:16.570 --> 01:25:21.450
that you may rise up and seize this moment
to take your victory.

977
01:25:21.534 --> 01:25:25.371
to take your justice
and to take your revenge!

978
01:25:44.390 --> 01:25:45.891
Zi Yuan.

979
01:25:50.187 --> 01:25:52.189
(SHOUTING)

980
01:25:52.273 --> 01:25:53.899
It's General Ming!

981
01:25:54.358 --> 01:25:55.943
Follow General Ming!

982
01:26:00.239 --> 01:26:03.409
Prepare for battle!

983
01:26:12.626 --> 01:26:15.588
These are...
They're good undead guys. right?

984
01:26:16.130 --> 01:26:19.175
Oh. no. no. no!

985
01:26:19.258 --> 01:26:21.552
Zi Yuan! Zi Yuan! Zi Yuan sent us!

986
01:26:21.635 --> 01:26:25.890
- Darling. I don't think he speaks English.
- RICK: We're with Zi Yuan!

987
01:26:25.973 --> 01:26:27.266
Zi Yuan?

988
01:26:27.808 --> 01:26:29.101
Right.

989
01:26:30.770 --> 01:26:32.063
Let's go.

990
01:26:33.064 --> 01:26:34.398
To battle!

991
01:26:38.611 --> 01:26:41.781
(GRUNTING)

992
01:26:54.960 --> 01:26:59.090
Freedom! Freedom! Freedom!

993
01:27:01.926 --> 01:27:03.469
Archers form up!

994
01:27:07.681 --> 01:27:08.974
Incoming!

995
01:27:22.279 --> 01:27:26.367
- Hey! That's my favorite blue shirt.
- I've always hated that shirt.

996
01:27:26.492 --> 01:27:28.744
(CHATTERING)

997
01:27:41.507 --> 01:27:42.550
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

998
01:27:42.675 --> 01:27:44.260
Death to General Ming!

999
01:27:48.264 --> 01:27:49.682
Charge!

1000
01:27:59.859 --> 01:28:02.027
Welcome to the 20th century!

1001
01:28:02.111 --> 01:28:04.864
(MACHINE GUN FIRING)

1002
01:28:17.710 --> 01:28:18.752
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

1003
01:28:18.878 --> 01:28:21.297
We can't let them cross the wall!

1004
01:28:55.247 --> 01:28:57.249
(GRUNTING)

1005
01:29:48.008 --> 01:29:49.468
You are no longer immortal.

1006
01:30:30.426 --> 01:30:33.178
Honey! Fall back to higher ground!

1007
01:30:39.852 --> 01:30:42.187
I really hate mummies!

1008
01:30:42.271 --> 01:30:44.607
It seems the feeling's mutual!

1009
01:30:48.360 --> 01:30:50.529
Shut up. clay boy! Fore!

1010
01:30:51.113 --> 01:30:52.281
Run!

1011
01:31:05.210 --> 01:31:06.795
- Catch!
- Got it!

1012
01:31:08.881 --> 01:31:13.218
Next time I say. "We've been in tougher
scrapes than this." I mean this!

1013
01:31:32.488 --> 01:31:35.074
(GUN FIRING)

1014
01:31:38.911 --> 01:31:42.206
Die. you mummy bastards! Die!

1015
01:31:42.289 --> 01:31:45.334
There is no call for bad language!

1016
01:31:47.586 --> 01:31:50.839
Jonathan certainly knows
how to make an entrance!

1017
01:32:17.449 --> 01:32:19.243
Any regrets. darling?

1018
01:32:21.370 --> 01:32:23.330
None. Not ever.

1019
01:32:32.756 --> 01:32:35.676
- You okay?
- Yeah. sure. no problem.

1020
01:32:35.759 --> 01:32:38.262
We had it completely under control.

1021
01:32:41.098 --> 01:32:43.809
This guy ever run out of tricks?

1022
01:32:48.188 --> 01:32:49.523
No!

1023
01:32:56.739 --> 01:32:58.240
Mother! No!

1024
01:33:01.076 --> 01:33:02.369
Mother!

1025
01:33:07.291 --> 01:33:09.585
Mother! Mother!

1026
01:33:19.887 --> 01:33:21.889
Pierce through his heart.

1027
01:33:24.725 --> 01:33:29.229
You must live and fight on.

1028
01:33:30.063 --> 01:33:31.857
(CRYING)

1029
01:33:48.624 --> 01:33:51.210
She said through the heart.

1030
01:33:51.293 --> 01:33:53.837
Through the heart. Let's go.

1031
01:34:06.600 --> 01:34:07.643
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

1032
01:34:07.726 --> 01:34:08.811
Get in!

1033
01:34:09.686 --> 01:34:12.397
The O'Connells are going to
stop the Emperor!

1034
01:34:24.034 --> 01:34:26.453
So. Dad. what's the plan?

1035
01:34:26.537 --> 01:34:28.038
Divide and conquer!

1036
01:34:28.121 --> 01:34:31.208
No offense.
but isn't that a little short on detail?

1037
01:34:31.917 --> 01:34:34.419
- Twelve o'clock low!
- Hang on!

1038
01:34:42.678 --> 01:34:44.096
Remember our deal!

1039
01:34:44.179 --> 01:34:46.807
When this is over.
my men get to drink for free!

1040
01:34:46.890 --> 01:34:49.810
You can have the whole damn bar
for all I care!

1041
01:34:49.893 --> 01:34:52.604
I'm getting the hell out of China.

1042
01:35:23.302 --> 01:35:24.344
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

1043
01:35:24.428 --> 01:35:26.889
I dug you up...

1044
01:35:27.806 --> 01:35:30.267
and I'm gonna put you down.

1045
01:35:45.032 --> 01:35:47.284
(SCREAMING)

1046
01:36:01.590 --> 01:36:04.343
Alex? Alex!

1047
01:36:24.905 --> 01:36:26.615
(GRUNTING)

1048
01:36:31.787 --> 01:36:33.664
(CHOKING)

1049
01:37:03.193 --> 01:37:04.236
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

1050
01:37:04.319 --> 01:37:05.404
Let go!

1051
01:37:05.487 --> 01:37:06.571
Never!

1052
01:37:10.492 --> 01:37:13.453
RICK: Enough tricks! Where's your honor?

1053
01:37:16.581 --> 01:37:18.291
Fight like a man!

1054
01:37:24.297 --> 01:37:26.216
(RICK GRUNTING)

1055
01:37:57.039 --> 01:37:58.707
Divide

1056
01:38:00.292 --> 01:38:01.752
and conquer.

1057
01:38:41.333 --> 01:38:43.543
(EMPEROR GROANING)

1058
01:38:48.423 --> 01:38:51.259
Now you can rule in hell.

1059
01:39:16.493 --> 01:39:17.536
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

1060
01:39:17.619 --> 01:39:19.371
The Emperor is dead.

1061
01:39:19.663 --> 01:39:21.331
The Emperor is dead!

1062
01:39:57.951 --> 01:40:00.370
(SINGING)

1063
01:40:08.253 --> 01:40:12.382
- Evening. girls. You're looking well.
- WOMAN: Good evening. Mr. Maguire.

1064
01:40:13.258 --> 01:40:17.053
- It's a fine night to be me.
- You dance great for an old lady.

1065
01:40:17.596 --> 01:40:20.140
Someone told me to stop living
on the sidelines.

1066
01:40:20.223 --> 01:40:23.268
- Well. he sounds like a smart guy.
- He is.

1067
01:40:35.280 --> 01:40:38.783
So I guess Dash and Scarlet
have their next adventure?

1068
01:40:38.867 --> 01:40:41.745
Why write about it when you can live it?

1069
01:40:42.871 --> 01:40:47.083
There's something incredibly romantic
about vanquishing the undead.

1070
01:40:47.918 --> 01:40:50.503
Even more romantic doing it with you.

1071
01:40:51.296 --> 01:40:54.132
- Kiss me.
- Don't have to ask me twice.

1072
01:41:03.266 --> 01:41:04.935
- Can I get your bag. sir?
- No. no. no.

1073
01:41:05.018 --> 01:41:07.020
Don't touch it. don't touch it.

1074
01:41:07.103 --> 01:41:08.146
Where are you off to. Mr. Carnahan?

1075
01:41:08.230 --> 01:41:10.607
Someplace where they don't have mummies.

1076
01:41:10.690 --> 01:41:13.526
- Step on it! I've got a plane to catch.
- DRIVER: Yes. sir.

1077
01:41:13.610 --> 01:41:17.280
Yeah. <i>Ciao. ciao.</i> Shanghai.

1078
01:41:17.364 --> 01:41:19.532
Peru. here I come.

1079
01:41:22.535 --> 01:41:26.998
Soon after. mummies were found in Peru.
